[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429522\">7005R35</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the electrical connection.</p><p>3. Keep the motor assembly.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045162.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the motor is undamaged.</p><p>Connect the electrical conneciton, position\nthe motor and fasten it using the bolts.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429522\">7005R35</a></p><p>Check that the mirror is working properly.</p>"]]